# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS AND CREDENTIALS - never commit these.
# NetGuard stores an encrypted secret blob plus its entropy key on disk. Both are
# machine-scoped and useless elsewhere, but committing either would publish the
# shape of your alerting setup and, on Linux, the key that protects it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
state/secrets.json
state/.ngkey
**/secrets.json
**/.ngkey
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
.env
.env.*

# Local configuration contains your webhook host, SMTP account and phone gateway.
# The committed template is config/netguard.config.example.json.
config/netguard.config.json
config/hub.txt
config/oui.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNTIME STATE - regenerated on every run, machine-specific, often large.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
state/
baseline/
logs/
reports/
evidence/
quarantine/

# Generated remediation scripts. These are produced by the hardening agent from
# the control catalogue and describe the specific weaknesses of one machine.
harden/Apply-Tier*.ps1
harden/Rollback-Tier*.ps1
harden/*.log
harden/apply-*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors, OS cruft, build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
out/
dist/
*.zip

# Test scratch
tests/tmp/
tests/*.tmp
TestResults*.xml
